WEBVTT

01:40.040 --> 01:42.290
Wow! Look at all the melon bread!

01:42.290 --> 01:44.660
Isn't <i>yakisoba </i>bread the clear winner?

01:55.790 --> 01:57.580
Hey there! I'm Yuu!

01:57.580 --> 01:58.620
I'm Nobu!

01:58.620 --> 02:00.750
Saving the world through comedy...

02:01.830 --> 02:04.620
--We're No Byuuun!
--We're No Byuuun!

02:04.620 --> 02:06.950
Wait! Why are you eating melon bread?

02:06.950 --> 02:09.080
Well, why do you have this?

02:10.620 --> 02:15.120
Hey, Nobu, why is it <i>yakisoba</i>
bread has <i>yakisoba </i>in it,

02:15.120 --> 02:18.540
but melon bread has no melon?

02:18.540 --> 02:23.370
That's because a melon would be
too big to fit inside the bun!

02:23.370 --> 02:26.500
Oh, is that why? Nobu, you're so smart!

02:26.500 --> 02:28.540
I'm just kidding.

02:29.660 --> 02:31.750
Oh, Mommy, can you hear me?

02:31.750 --> 02:33.790
What? I'm with my friends.

02:33.790 --> 02:34.870
Yeah.

02:34.870 --> 02:37.700
I hope you can come get us soon.

02:37.700 --> 02:39.330
Mommy, are you listening?

02:39.330 --> 02:41.910
Mommy? Are you okay, Mommy?

02:43.700 --> 02:45.830
I see, young lady. To Osaka it is.

02:45.830 --> 02:48.790
Vroom, vroom, here we go!

02:48.790 --> 02:51.120
That's a motorcycle, not a taxi!

02:51.120 --> 02:53.790
And stop hitting on her!

02:53.790 --> 02:55.620
Mommy, what's wrong?

02:55.620 --> 02:57.330
Mommy, I can't hear you!

02:57.330 --> 03:00.250
Mommy, don't use a creepy voice!

03:00.250 --> 03:02.370
Don't hang up, Mommy!

03:02.370 --> 03:03.870
Meg.

03:06.120 --> 03:10.330
This is Student Council President
Kazuma Aoike.

03:10.330 --> 03:12.200
The first floor is not safe.

03:12.200 --> 03:15.790
Everyone healthy should
move to a higher floor.

03:15.790 --> 03:20.330
President, I've got a feeling
this will be an amazing documentary!

03:20.330 --> 03:22.580
Kiriko, get this angle, too!

03:22.580 --> 03:24.290
Remain calm.

03:24.290 --> 03:28.910
Upperclassmen, look after the underclassmen.

03:31.120 --> 03:34.790
If we trust each other and help each other,

03:34.790 --> 03:37.870
we can overcome this situation.

03:42.330 --> 03:45.000
The brass band is working hard.

03:45.000 --> 03:47.660
Then let's do our part, too.

03:49.620 --> 03:52.450
But see, there's an entire
banana roll cake,

03:52.450 --> 03:54.500
but there's no such thing
as an entire melon roll, is there?

03:54.500 --> 03:57.330
I told you, a melon would be too big.

03:57.330 --> 03:59.950
Oh, so that <i>was </i>it.

04:01.540 --> 04:03.410
Big Sis.

04:05.290 --> 04:08.120
Student president.

04:08.120 --> 04:11.870
The roof is not
the <i>rakugo </i>club's playground!

04:11.870 --> 04:14.250
Isn't that right, President?

04:14.250 --> 04:16.580
It's a stress release.

04:16.580 --> 04:17.950
We're detoxing.

04:17.950 --> 04:20.120
We're <i>relaxing</i>!

04:20.120 --> 04:22.910
Regardless, I'm glad to see you're okay.

04:22.910 --> 04:27.580
And I see Takamori and Ikari from
the softball team are okay, too.

04:30.790 --> 04:34.000
I'm Megumi, from the manga club.

04:34.000 --> 04:36.540
Benishima from the go home club.

04:36.540 --> 04:37.950
Hope I'm not intruding.

04:38.200 --> 04:42.830
"Science Lab System"

04:43.750 --> 04:45.250
Film it, Kiriko!

04:45.250 --> 04:47.250
P-President!

04:51.200 --> 04:52.370
Film it.

04:55.290 --> 04:59.160
Make... the ultimate documentary.

05:11.410 --> 05:13.750
President! President Kaihara!

05:17.250 --> 05:20.040
She's not breathing!

05:20.040 --> 05:21.660
President...

05:34.450 --> 05:37.160
"School Route"

05:34.450 --> 05:37.160
She came back to life.

05:37.160 --> 05:39.500
--So why did you--
--No.

05:39.500 --> 05:43.950
She was bitten and died.
That wasn't Kaihara anymore.

05:43.950 --> 05:47.120
It was something else.

05:47.120 --> 05:49.750
But... But...

05:56.540 --> 05:58.950
If you're bitten, once you die...

05:58.950 --> 06:01.080
...you become something else.

06:01.080 --> 06:03.790
Then that thing bites someone else,

06:03.790 --> 06:08.080
who dies, turns,
and bites yet another person.

06:08.080 --> 06:12.330
By now, the second floor is probably
full of those who were bitten.

06:12.330 --> 06:14.160
No way...

06:14.160 --> 06:17.700
They were probably bitten before
going to the second floor, and then...

06:21.040 --> 06:27.950
Then they died, turned into something else,
and bit into some other student...

06:27.950 --> 06:28.950
President...

06:28.950 --> 06:30.910
Why do they bite?

06:34.290 --> 06:36.330
That's...

06:36.330 --> 06:38.580
...how they eat.

06:38.580 --> 06:39.950
No!

06:39.950 --> 06:43.160
Those stains... Weren't you two bitten?

06:43.160 --> 06:46.120
You'll end up like the others.

06:46.120 --> 06:48.160
This?

06:48.160 --> 06:52.700
This blood got on me
when I tried to save Kaihara.

06:52.700 --> 06:54.040
Is that true?

06:54.040 --> 06:56.700
The President died from being bitten!

06:56.700 --> 06:59.620
Then she turned into someone else...

06:59.620 --> 07:02.410
This is her blood!

07:03.450 --> 07:04.950
Sorry.

07:04.950 --> 07:07.080
I believe Kiriko about her bloodstains.

07:07.080 --> 07:08.410
But Benishima...

07:08.410 --> 07:09.830
Drop it, Kaoru.

07:11.830 --> 07:13.750
I'm taking a smoke break.

07:18.290 --> 07:20.250
Student Council President!

07:21.290 --> 07:22.700
Hikami.

07:22.700 --> 07:26.370
The science club is creating
a bomb in the science lab.

07:27.910 --> 07:29.160
Hey, hey,

07:29.160 --> 07:33.700
that girl Hikami from the science club
was really busy, huh?

07:33.700 --> 07:36.080
After telling us she'd signal
when the bomb was ready

07:36.080 --> 07:38.950
so we could blow those things
away and escape,

07:38.950 --> 07:42.120
she just grabbed a bag of chips
and went back to the lab.

07:43.830 --> 07:47.910
The brass band members said
this would be finally be the year

07:47.910 --> 07:51.120
they won the prefectural
tournament and go to nationals.

07:51.120 --> 07:55.830
No Byun's goal is to save
the world through comedy.

07:55.830 --> 07:58.450
Yeah, world peace.

07:58.450 --> 08:04.910
But once someone's bitten... they get
hungry even though they're dead.

08:04.910 --> 08:09.540
I kinda feel bad for them.

08:09.540 --> 08:14.450
Nobu, if that happens to you,
you can eat me.

08:14.450 --> 08:17.200
Are you some kind of white knight?

08:20.080 --> 08:21.700
Yuu, that fall was ridiculous!

08:24.330 --> 08:27.080
You two aren't scared?

08:28.250 --> 08:32.700
Meg, you want to be a manga author
when you grow up, right?

08:32.700 --> 08:35.870
Yeah! I'm gonna
draw manga about Mr. Ribbit.

08:35.870 --> 08:37.160
Right, Mr. Ribbit?

08:37.160 --> 08:38.370
That's ribbight.

08:38.370 --> 08:42.330
--Our dream is to save the world
through comedy.
--Our dream is to save the world
through comedy.

08:42.330 --> 08:44.000
--No Byuuun!
--No Byuuun!

08:44.000 --> 08:46.250
Hey, Big Sis.

08:48.200 --> 08:51.580
Your dream still hasn't changed, right?

08:51.580 --> 08:54.000
Wh-Why bring that up all of a sudden?

08:54.000 --> 08:58.290
Why do you call her that?
You're not sisters, right?

08:58.290 --> 09:02.500
Oh, well our houses are right next
to each other, so I grew up calling her that.

09:02.500 --> 09:04.000
Ah-ha.

09:04.000 --> 09:07.000
When we were really little,
we played together all the time!

09:14.370 --> 09:16.700
Big Sis would be a pop idol,

09:16.700 --> 09:19.540
and I'd be her fan!
I'd cheer for her.

09:24.950 --> 09:27.830
The student council president's
dream is to be a pop idol.

09:27.830 --> 09:31.620
That's... something I can't even imagine.

09:33.040 --> 09:34.830
No one's coming for us.

09:34.830 --> 09:37.040
Yup. Nobody's coming.

09:40.160 --> 09:43.950
I thought rescue might come
if I uploaded a video,

09:43.950 --> 09:45.950
but my battery's dead!

09:47.700 --> 09:49.790
Outdoor outlet located.

09:49.790 --> 09:52.160
I saw the other part earlier.

09:52.160 --> 09:54.750
Time for No Byun to move out, Yuu.

09:54.830 --> 10:01.830
"School Route"

10:21.410 --> 10:24.700
There was a charger
in the teacher's desk, right?

10:24.700 --> 10:26.870
Yeah, there was.

10:32.910 --> 10:34.750
Looks like no one's there.

10:34.750 --> 10:36.080
Hey.

10:37.950 --> 10:41.950
There's something
I've been meaning to ask you.

10:41.950 --> 10:43.450
What is it?

10:43.450 --> 10:48.290
Nobu, what made you
decide to do <i>manzai </i>with me?

10:48.290 --> 10:51.660
Huh? Why do you ask?

10:53.040 --> 10:57.160
I mean, I'm a weirdo, aren't I?

11:19.410 --> 11:23.120
♬ Up on the roof ♬

11:23.120 --> 11:26.080
--♬ In the glow of sunset ♬
--Yeah. You're weird all right.

11:29.040 --> 11:34.040
I thought, if I'm gonna team up with someone,
not normal should be better.

11:41.330 --> 11:43.120
But the truth is,

11:43.120 --> 11:47.160
it's because you would sometimes
get a lonely look on your face.

11:48.950 --> 11:51.540
That's what drew my attention.

11:56.410 --> 11:59.950
Yuu, I didn't realize your mother was gone.

11:59.950 --> 12:01.500
Sorry.

12:02.410 --> 12:04.000
It's fine.

12:04.000 --> 12:06.290
It happened a long time ago.

12:06.290 --> 12:10.950
Besides, even now, my mom's death
hasn't really hit me.

12:12.660 --> 12:16.700
The moment I was told my mom died,
know what I thought?

12:21.370 --> 12:24.870
"What am I, some kind of
fairy tale protagonist?"

12:28.500 --> 12:32.620
Also, my mom was hospitalized
the whole time,

12:32.620 --> 12:35.250
so it became normal
for her not to be around.

12:43.040 --> 12:44.790
Nobu, are you gonna cry?

12:46.790 --> 12:50.250
You can't cry or you'll break the spell.

12:51.580 --> 12:53.120
Okay, I get it.

12:54.660 --> 12:58.200
As long as I keep making everyone laugh,
the spell won't break.

12:58.620 --> 13:01.950
Okay, okay. I know.

13:01.950 --> 13:05.200
I'm gonna be a fairy tale princess forever.

13:05.910 --> 13:09.950
So I'm gonna study <i>manzai </i>even more.

13:10.950 --> 13:13.830
What's important in <i>manzai </i>is aberration.

13:13.830 --> 13:18.040
It's not aberration. It's <i>articulation</i>!

13:18.040 --> 13:20.620
The tip of the tong,
the teas, and the lisps.

13:21.290 --> 13:23.410
You said that wrong!

13:23.410 --> 13:26.500
The tip of the tongue,
the teeth, and the lips.

13:32.750 --> 13:36.160
That convinced me I was right.

13:36.160 --> 13:38.870
I don't see any of those people.

13:38.870 --> 13:40.750
Did you say something?

13:40.750 --> 13:42.330
It's a secret.

14:24.370 --> 14:27.080
This girl's not moving.

14:31.950 --> 14:35.540
Maybe she didn't eat despite being hungry.

14:42.500 --> 14:44.750
Who could that be playing?

15:14.410 --> 15:17.250
Isn't that Shigemoto from class B?

15:17.250 --> 15:21.250
Oh, I heard she won some fancy competition.

15:26.160 --> 15:28.160
Sorry for interrupting.

15:29.410 --> 15:33.410
Don't be. I'm glad there was
someone to hear me play.

15:33.410 --> 15:36.540
Listen, um, it's not safe here anymore.

15:39.540 --> 15:41.120
You can come to the roof.

15:41.120 --> 15:43.910
We have food and water.

15:46.410 --> 15:48.330
Thanks.

15:48.330 --> 15:51.580
But right now, I want to keep
playing the piano.

16:01.120 --> 16:02.450
Found it!

16:02.450 --> 16:04.160
We did it!

16:07.330 --> 16:10.040
We need to help her, don't we?

16:28.120 --> 16:30.200
Um, Shigemoto,

16:30.200 --> 16:32.660
please come with us.

16:36.160 --> 16:37.870
Shigemoto!

16:57.790 --> 16:59.370
Nobu...

17:11.620 --> 17:12.870
Nobu!

17:15.080 --> 17:16.330
Nobu!

17:59.750 --> 18:01.370
Hey!

18:06.290 --> 18:08.040
The helicopter's leaving!

18:14.120 --> 18:15.790
That's the one we just saw.

18:21.250 --> 18:24.330
They're all moving toward the helicopter.

18:36.750 --> 18:38.830
It's too dangerous.

18:41.410 --> 18:45.450
"School Route"

18:49.660 --> 18:52.870
I guess no one's coming to save us.

18:56.120 --> 18:59.790
Well, the helicopter did crash.

18:59.790 --> 19:01.750
Yeah.

19:18.290 --> 19:21.950
I wonder if help is really coming.

19:27.160 --> 19:30.870
If not, we'll eventually be attacked...

19:30.870 --> 19:33.370
...or run out of food and starve.

19:35.790 --> 19:38.950
Either way, we die.

19:40.700 --> 19:42.040
I'm useless.

19:42.040 --> 19:47.250
We can't afford to have an indecisive
student council president right now.

19:47.250 --> 19:50.200
You aren't useless at all.

19:50.200 --> 19:56.000
You don't know how reassuring it is
just to have you here with us.

20:00.290 --> 20:01.950
Thanks.

20:05.330 --> 20:07.040
This is good.

20:08.620 --> 20:11.620
"Cream Bread"        "Fruit Mix Gummies"

20:15.620 --> 20:17.040
Hungry?

20:22.120 --> 20:23.450
No.

20:23.450 --> 20:25.040
Okay, then.

20:26.160 --> 20:30.500
Benishima, stay away from Takamori.

20:30.500 --> 20:32.040
Why?

20:32.040 --> 20:35.120
Why? You know why.

20:35.120 --> 20:37.580
Because you were kicked off
the team for smoking,

20:37.580 --> 20:40.700
we couldn't enter the summer tournament.

20:43.200 --> 20:45.450
Whoa. Benishima...

20:45.450 --> 20:47.660
...was on the softball team.

20:48.500 --> 20:54.410
You and Captain Takamori are so good,
people called you the Golden Battery.

20:55.450 --> 20:59.290
Yet it was all gone in an instant!

21:00.450 --> 21:03.080
You shattered our dreams!

21:04.250 --> 21:05.790
Stop it, Kaoru.

21:05.790 --> 21:07.290
But--!

21:09.660 --> 21:12.950
Mommy, Daddy, get here soon!

21:12.950 --> 21:16.870
Everyone's mental health
is about to be a serious problem.

21:20.700 --> 21:23.000
Let's go to the mall.

21:23.000 --> 21:27.120
They said it was turned into a shelter.

21:28.370 --> 21:33.370
Once night falls,
rescue might not be possible.

21:33.370 --> 21:36.660
If we try to leave, we'll be attacked.

21:36.660 --> 21:39.540
If we stay here, we'll eventually be attacked.

21:39.540 --> 21:43.040
So let's launch a preemptive strike.

21:43.040 --> 21:46.040
Then what's our plan of attack?

21:50.120 --> 21:52.410
First, we break that fence.

21:52.410 --> 21:54.580
By blowing it up, right?

21:54.580 --> 21:56.080
Yes.

21:56.080 --> 21:57.580
After that...

22:02.370 --> 22:05.330
After that, we slip through the remains
of the old school building...

22:06.830 --> 22:08.370
...and enter the woods.

22:08.370 --> 22:10.500
We'll cut through the woods...

22:11.870 --> 22:14.580
...and head for the mall.

22:15.580 --> 22:19.410
I see. I forgot about using
the old school building.

22:19.410 --> 22:22.700
And those things are much
less likely to be in the woods.

22:22.700 --> 22:24.790
I know the way through.

22:24.790 --> 22:29.910
You used to cut through the woods during
practice to go eat croquettes pretty often.

22:31.450 --> 22:35.370
Nobu, where are you hiding?

22:35.370 --> 22:39.250
You're not thinking up jokes
without me, are you?

22:39.250 --> 22:41.330
Where are you hiding?

22:47.120 --> 22:49.160
Found you, Nobu!

22:51.790 --> 22:54.250
Nobu, what's wrong?

22:55.250 --> 22:58.410
I just feel so weak.

22:58.410 --> 23:00.580
Do you have a fever?

23:02.540 --> 23:04.000
That's the wrong forehead!

23:07.620 --> 23:09.040
No fever.

23:09.040 --> 23:10.870
Actually, you're kinda cold.

23:10.870 --> 23:13.660
Huh. Then I guess I'm fine.

23:18.200 --> 23:20.250
Hikami's signaling us.

23:20.250 --> 23:22.040
The bomb is ready, then.

23:22.040 --> 23:23.450
All right. I'll go get it.

23:23.450 --> 23:26.790
No, Yumiya, I'll go. I'm faster than you.

23:30.080 --> 23:32.160
We should get moving, too.

23:49.750 --> 23:52.200
--Hey, Manzai Duo, you're gonna get left behind.
--D-Don't worry.

23:52.200 --> 23:54.250
Go on ahead. We'll catch up.

23:54.250 --> 23:56.500
Come on, Nobu. Let's go.

23:56.500 --> 23:57.870
Nobu--

24:13.250 --> 24:15.160
You all go ahead.

24:15.160 --> 24:20.000
I need to make an announcement
for anyone left telling them to evacuate.

24:20.000 --> 24:21.580
I'll go with you.

24:21.580 --> 24:26.290
No. I need you to support
everyone in my place.

24:26.290 --> 24:27.580
But...

24:27.580 --> 24:32.870
We need to hurry to make
our rendezvous with Takamori.

24:32.870 --> 24:35.200
President, I want to stay...

24:35.200 --> 24:39.830
Shizuka, get going. That's an order
from your Student Council President.

24:41.160 --> 24:42.620
Yes, ma'am!

24:59.660 --> 25:02.160
Take it...

25:02.160 --> 25:03.660
...and go...

25:05.330 --> 25:07.040
Hikami...

25:20.200 --> 25:21.910
That surprised me.

25:21.910 --> 25:27.200
All of a sudden, I felt woozy
and then I went whoosh-thud.

25:27.200 --> 25:30.790
Nobu, that wasn't all for a joke, was it?

25:30.790 --> 25:34.080
Oh, Yuu's mad.

25:34.080 --> 25:36.000
I'm not mad.

25:47.660 --> 25:49.160
Nobu.

25:55.950 --> 25:59.870
Yuu, what made you want
to team up with me?

26:02.040 --> 26:03.750
Well, it's because...

26:04.830 --> 26:08.500
I'm a weirdo!

26:08.500 --> 26:12.080
That's not the real answer.

26:12.080 --> 26:14.330
It was because...

26:14.330 --> 26:15.910
Nobu?

26:15.910 --> 26:17.410
Because...

26:19.290 --> 26:22.540
Because I'm a lonely girl. Right?

26:23.950 --> 26:25.790
Nobu.

26:25.790 --> 26:28.950
My reactions were too sharp,
and no matter who I paired with,

26:28.950 --> 26:31.330
it didn't work.

26:32.830 --> 26:36.200
But you always responded with a smile.

26:39.660 --> 26:43.660
It was because I was lonely, like you.

26:56.540 --> 27:00.790
Attention, everyone. This is Student Council
President Kazuma Aoike.

27:07.290 --> 27:11.580
Anyone who's still uninjured,
head for the old school building.

27:11.580 --> 27:15.500
Anyone who can escape,
head for the old school building.

27:29.370 --> 27:32.660
Already, many of them can't move.

27:32.660 --> 27:35.200
This may make escape feasible--

27:44.040 --> 27:48.830
I captured the decisive moment, President...

27:50.620 --> 27:55.370
Today, we lost many friends.

27:55.370 --> 27:59.500
There are still more painful
and difficult things ahead.

28:16.830 --> 28:18.910
Takamori!

28:18.910 --> 28:20.370
Asayo!

28:28.330 --> 28:29.870
Asayo!

28:29.870 --> 28:31.200
Crap.

28:38.250 --> 28:41.000
Asayo!

28:41.000 --> 28:43.910
I'm sorry, Yumiya.

28:45.120 --> 28:51.200
Back then, I succumbed to the pressure
of being captain and smoked.

28:52.660 --> 28:55.790
And yet you took the fall.

28:58.450 --> 29:00.410
Benishima! Throw me your lighter!

29:00.410 --> 29:02.620
I'll take them out with a bang!

29:02.620 --> 29:04.660
Shut up! Don't say that!

29:05.870 --> 29:09.660
This time, let <i>me </i>protect <i>you</i>.

29:12.330 --> 29:13.910
Asayo...

29:16.040 --> 29:20.700
Takamori, you haven't lost
your touch, right?

29:41.250 --> 29:43.000
Run!

29:53.700 --> 29:55.870
Looks like the bomb worked.

30:02.580 --> 30:05.580
But all of you remember...

30:05.580 --> 30:09.410
...your dreams.

30:09.410 --> 30:16.000
Even if they don't come true,
our dreams will give us strength

30:16.000 --> 30:19.200
in the toughest, most painful times.

30:19.200 --> 30:24.750
And remember the dreams
of the friends you lost.

30:24.750 --> 30:27.410
Nobu, are you hungry?

30:27.410 --> 30:29.830
You can eat me.

30:30.750 --> 30:33.000
I don't like bean paste bread.

30:33.000 --> 30:35.450
I'm <i>yakisoba </i>bread.

30:36.700 --> 30:38.620
Then shall I have you?

30:43.620 --> 30:45.330
That's enough.

30:49.250 --> 30:51.830
Thank you for everything.

30:55.500 --> 30:57.080
Nobu?

31:24.290 --> 31:29.410
♬ However much I wish,
however much I wish ♬

31:29.410 --> 31:35.120
♬ My dream might always lie
beyond my grasp ♬

31:35.120 --> 31:40.580
♬ Despite that, because I have you ♬

31:40.580 --> 31:45.290
♬ No matter what the future brings ♬

31:45.290 --> 31:49.500
♬ I can walk forward ♬

31:52.160 --> 31:54.830
♬ It's a funny thing ♬

31:54.830 --> 31:59.620
♬ I started wanting to believe in destiny ♬

31:59.620 --> 32:03.120
♬ From the moment I met you ♬

32:03.120 --> 32:05.000
--♬ I was a prisoner of the past ♬

32:05.000 --> 32:05.830
--Nobu?
--♬ I was a prisoner of the past ♬

32:05.830 --> 32:06.790
-- ♬ I was shouting for someone
to let me out the whole time ♬

32:06.790 --> 32:08.450
-- Nobu!
-- ♬ I was shouting for someone
to let me out the whole time ♬

32:08.450 --> 32:14.080
-- ♬ I was shouting for someone
to let me out the whole time ♬

32:14.080 --> 32:19.120
♬ After sharing a secret
I couldn't tell anyone ♬

32:19.120 --> 32:24.830
♬ Hey, when people talk about bonds,
this is what they mean, isn't it ♬

32:43.830 --> 32:47.120
Nobu, you waited?

32:48.870 --> 32:52.160
You silly goof. I'm over here.

32:54.040 --> 32:56.000
Nobu!

32:56.000 --> 32:58.200
This thing isn't me.

33:02.000 --> 33:05.910
I told you I'd always stick with you.

33:05.910 --> 33:10.290
But, Nobu, you left me.

33:10.290 --> 33:11.450
Did you know?

33:11.450 --> 33:15.870
In <i>manzai</i>, the funny man is
more popular than the straight man.

33:17.450 --> 33:20.790
So, Yuu, even solo,
you'll be entertaining.

33:20.790 --> 33:24.660
But it's even better with you, Nobu!

33:26.500 --> 33:29.540
Didn't you hear me?
I'll always be with you.

33:45.950 --> 33:47.620
Here.

33:48.370 --> 33:49.950
I see.

33:49.950 --> 33:53.790
So even solo, I'm still No Byun.

33:58.160 --> 34:01.250
Yeah. Saving the world through comedy...

34:04.120 --> 34:06.700
--...we're No Byuuun!
--...we're No Byuuun!

34:11.370 --> 34:14.410
I can't save the world staying here.

34:14.410 --> 34:17.500
There's no one to laugh.

35:02.700 --> 35:04.450
Now then,

35:04.450 --> 35:06.540
where shall I go?
